I really think they missed out by not having more manufacturers on display. The Motorola Stylus line has been fantastic for me: All day battery life, decent performance, and decent cameras. What sets that line of phones apart is that they are the smartphones that I know of available in any western market that retain headphone jacks and expandable storage while also implementing modern must-have features like OLED high refresh rate screens and wireless charging. I haven't used the stylus much but it is completely serviceable and integrated in the phone. And despite all these features, it's still a decent size and form factor.  
All of these upsides and more for the low, low price of ~$500 USD. 
@Linus, might be worth a looksie. I think this would be perfect for Yvonne.
